---
/**
 * Markdown tables are wrapped in a scroll container automatically — see the
 * `components` map passed to <Content /> — so a wide table never widens the page
 * and authors never have to remember to wrap one.
 *
 * The wrapper is a focusable region rather than `display: block` on the table
 * itself, which would strip the table role from the accessibility tree.
 */
---

<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Table" tabindex="0">
  <table><slot /></table>
</div>
